What a year of urban drift-scan reveals — the science atop the astro pipeline, and the sampling theory that makes it possible.

The science / insight strand of the astro estate: the long-horizon question everything else scaffolds — *what does a year-scale, long-baseline urban astronomy dataset yield?* — and the connective theory that answers it. It is a development strand (an open research frontier, STATE is a moving frontier), above the per-camera keepers (astro-polecam, astro-eclipticam, astro-canon) and the data keeper (astro-storage). It does not own capture or plumbing; it owns the *ideas that turn accumulated frames into named, measured stars*, and the public face those results reach (the `/astro` web deliverables).
